\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Elitzur’s local average and the neutral Gauss constraint}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{In a compact Abelian lattice model with site and link angles,
\citet{§I, pp. 3979–3980}{elitzur1975local} studies the cosine of a
link angle. A gauge change at one site leaves the action invariant.
Only source terms near that site vary in the orbit integral.
Elitzur bounds the expectation uniformly in the lattice size. We
cite his volume-limit conclusion that the expectation vanishes when
the external source is then removed. His compact-group argument uses a local observable whose
single-site orbit average vanishes. For a global rotation the
source changes at a number of sites growing with the volume
(§II, pp. 3980–3981). The finite site estimate in \ref{fdip-010R}
computes the response of a scalar vector to its own source.}

\p{The neutral Gauss constraint of \ref{fdip-008A} selects invariant
states in the complex Hilbert space of spatial links. In that
setting normalized Haar averaging is an orthogonal projection.
For the joint observable in \ref{fdip-010M}, the corresponding
averaging identity is algebraic when the group order is a unit.
The fixed-submodule conclusion for a site in \ref{fdip-010N}
already follows from a change of summation variable.}
